.TH "EPX\-PAYMENT\-TRANSACTIONS" "1" "" "epx" "epx manual"
.SH "NAME"
epx\-payment\-transactions \- read payment transactions; authorize, capture, refund and cancel payments
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.RS "4"
.nf
epx payment\-transactions [flags]
epx payment\-transactions [command]
.fi
.RE
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
Reads payment transactions, personal data included, and runs payments through the tenant\(aqs payment providers: authorize starts a transaction for an order, capture collects an authorized amount, refund returns a captured one and cancel voids an authorization. Capture, refund and cancel move money.
.PP
Its reads require the payment\-gateway.paymenttransactions_read scope. Its writes require different OAuth scopes; the help of each names them.
.SH "COMMANDS"
.SS "epx payment\-transactions authorize"
Authorize a payment.
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx payment\-transactions authorize [flags]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Authorizes the payment of an order with a payment mode, as \fB\-\-file\fR, a JSON object, gives them: order.id, paymentModeId, amountToAuthorize and currency, and what the provider needs, such as creditCardToken. The provider reserves the amount, which capture then collects. Emporix answers with the paymentTransactionId and, where the customer must finish the payment with the provider, where to send them (externalPaymentRedirectURL).
.PP
Emporix answers whether the operation succeeded (successful). epx prints the response and exits with 1 unless it says that it did: where it says that it failed (successful false, with a message), and where it does not say, when it may have been carried out all the same.
.PP
Changes data: on a terminal, epx asks before it sends POST. \fB\-\-yes\fR sends without asking (required without a terminal, or with \fB\-\-file\fR \-); \fB\-\-dry\-run\fR prints the request instead of sending it.
.PP
Requires the payment\-gateway.authorize_manage scope.
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Print the request instead of sending it (excludes \fB\-o\fR).
.TP
\fB\-\-file <PATH>\fR
JSON request body in PATH, sent byte for byte (\- reads standard input; sending it then needs \fB\-\-yes\fR; required).
.TP
\fB\-o, \-\-output <format>\fR
Format of the response: json or yaml. Default: \fBjson\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-yes\fR
Send without asking (required without a terminal, or with \fB\-\-file\fR \-).
.PP
\fBExamples:\fR
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx payment\-transactions authorize \-\-file authorize.json \-\-dry\-run
.fi
.RE
.SS "epx payment\-transactions cancel"
Cancel an authorized payment.
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx payment\-transactions cancel ID [flags]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Cancels the authorized payment of transaction ID: the provider releases the amount that it reserved.
.PP
This moves money: the confirmation names the transaction in the URL that it shows. ID is the ID that \fBepx payment\-transactions list\fR shows; an unknown one is not found (exit 4).
.PP
Emporix answers whether the operation succeeded (successful). epx prints the response and exits with 1 unless it says that it did: where it says that it failed (successful false, with a message), and where it does not say, when it may have been carried out all the same.
.PP
Changes data: on a terminal, epx asks before it sends POST. \fB\-\-yes\fR sends without asking (required without a terminal); \fB\-\-dry\-run\fR prints the request instead of sending it.
.PP
Requires the payment\-gateway.cancel_manage scope.
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Print the request instead of sending it (excludes \fB\-o\fR).
.TP
\fB\-o, \-\-output <format>\fR
Format of the response: json or yaml. Default: \fBjson\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-yes\fR
Send without asking (required without a terminal).
.PP
\fBExamples:\fR
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx payment\-transactions cancel T1 \-\-dry\-run
.fi
.RE
.SS "epx payment\-transactions capture"
Capture an authorized payment.
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx payment\-transactions capture ID [flags]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Captures \fB\-\-amount\fR in \fB\-\-currency\fR of the authorized payment of transaction ID, at most the amount authorized: the provider collects it from the customer. Emporix answers with the provider\(aqs captureId, which refund \fB\-\-capture\-id\fR takes.
.PP
This moves money: the confirmation names the transaction in the URL that it shows. ID is the ID that \fBepx payment\-transactions list\fR shows; an unknown one is not found (exit 4).
.PP
Emporix answers whether the operation succeeded (successful). epx prints the response and exits with 1 unless it says that it did: where it says that it failed (successful false, with a message), and where it does not say, when it may have been carried out all the same.
.PP
Changes data: on a terminal, epx asks before it sends POST. \fB\-\-yes\fR sends without asking (required without a terminal, or with \fB\-\-file\fR \-); \fB\-\-dry\-run\fR prints the request instead of sending it.
.PP
Requires the payment\-gateway.capture_manage scope.
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-amount <AMOUNT>\fR
The AMOUNT to capture, e.g. 3.99 (required without \fB\-\-file\fR).
.TP
\fB\-\-currency <CURRENCY>\fR
The CURRENCY of \fB\-\-amount\fR, e.g. EUR (required without \fB\-\-file\fR).
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Print the request instead of sending it (excludes \fB\-o\fR).
.TP
\fB\-\-file <PATH>\fR
JSON request body in PATH, sent byte for byte instead of the one that epx makes (\- reads standard input; sending it then needs \fB\-\-yes\fR).
.TP
\fB\-o, \-\-output <format>\fR
Format of the response: json or yaml. Default: \fBjson\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-yes\fR
Send without asking (required without a terminal, or with \fB\-\-file\fR \-).
.PP
\fBExamples:\fR
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx payment\-transactions capture T1 \-\-amount 3.99 \-\-currency EUR \-\-dry\-run
.fi
.RE
.SS "epx payment\-transactions get"
Show one payment transaction.
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx payment\-transactions get ID [flags]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Reads payment transactions, personal data included. PAYMENT MODE is the id of the payment mode used, and ENTRIES the operations the provider ran, in the order sent: type and amount, marked failed when they failed. Payment details (such as bank details and pay\-by\-link URLs), card tokens and the provider\(aqs requests and responses are only in \fB\-o json\fR. list\(aqs \fB\-\-sort\fR takes only createdDate (e.g. createdDate:desc); Emporix rejects other and several fields.
.PP
Requires the payment\-gateway.paymenttransactions_read scope.
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-columns <names>\fR
Print only these columns of table and csv, in this order: comma\-separated names (any case) among ID, PROVIDER, PAYMENT MODE, ENTRIES.
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-headers\fR
Print table and csv without the header row.
.TP
\fB\-o, \-\-output <format>\fR
Output format: table, json, yaml or csv (csv: the table\(aqs rows; json and yaml: the whole response). Default: \fBtable\fR.
.SS "epx payment\-transactions list"
List payment transactions.
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx payment\-transactions list [flags]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Reads payment transactions, personal data included. PAYMENT MODE is the id of the payment mode used, and ENTRIES the operations the provider ran, in the order sent: type and amount, marked failed when they failed. Payment details (such as bank details and pay\-by\-link URLs), card tokens and the provider\(aqs requests and responses are only in \fB\-o json\fR. list\(aqs \fB\-\-sort\fR takes only createdDate (e.g. createdDate:desc); Emporix rejects other and several fields.
.PP
Requires the payment\-gateway.paymenttransactions_read scope.
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-columns <names>\fR
Print only these columns of table and csv, in this order: comma\-separated names (any case) among ID, PROVIDER, PAYMENT MODE, ENTRIES.
.TP
\fB\-\-limit <n>\fR
Print at most n items; paged reads stop early where they safely can (0: every item).
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-headers\fR
Print table and csv without the header row.
.TP
\fB\-o, \-\-output <format>\fR
Output format: table, json, yaml or csv (csv: the table\(aqs rows; json and yaml: the whole response). Default: \fBtable\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-sort <order>\fR
Emporix sort order, passed as given: createdDate only, e.g. createdDate:desc; another field, or several, is refused (400, exit 1).
.TP
\fB\-\-stream\fR
Print items as JSON Lines as soon as they are checked, page by page on paged lists, reading up to 10000 pages where a list without it stops after 1000: a check failing on a later page exits 1 after the pages before it (excludes \fB\-o\fR, \fB\-\-columns\fR and \fB\-\-no\-headers\fR).
.SS "epx payment\-transactions refund"
Refund a captured payment.
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx payment\-transactions refund ID [flags]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Refunds \fB\-\-amount\fR in \fB\-\-currency\fR of the captured payment of transaction ID, at most the amount captured: the provider returns it to the customer. Where the payment was captured more than once, \fB\-\-capture\-id\fR names the capture to refund.
.PP
This moves money: the confirmation names the transaction in the URL that it shows. ID is the ID that \fBepx payment\-transactions list\fR shows; an unknown one is not found (exit 4).
.PP
Emporix answers whether the operation succeeded (successful). epx prints the response and exits with 1 unless it says that it did: where it says that it failed (successful false, with a message), and where it does not say, when it may have been carried out all the same.
.PP
Changes data: on a terminal, epx asks before it sends POST. \fB\-\-yes\fR sends without asking (required without a terminal, or with \fB\-\-file\fR \-); \fB\-\-dry\-run\fR prints the request instead of sending it.
.PP
Requires the payment\-gateway.refund_manage scope.
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-amount <AMOUNT>\fR
The AMOUNT to refund, e.g. 3.99 (required without \fB\-\-file\fR).
.TP
\fB\-\-capture\-id <ID>\fR
The ID of the capture to refund, as capture answered it.
.TP
\fB\-\-currency <CURRENCY>\fR
The CURRENCY of \fB\-\-amount\fR, e.g. EUR (required without \fB\-\-file\fR).
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Print the request instead of sending it (excludes \fB\-o\fR).
.TP
\fB\-\-file <PATH>\fR
JSON request body in PATH, sent byte for byte instead of the one that epx makes (\- reads standard input; sending it then needs \fB\-\-yes\fR).
.TP
\fB\-o, \-\-output <format>\fR
Format of the response: json or yaml. Default: \fBjson\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-yes\fR
Send without asking (required without a terminal, or with \fB\-\-file\fR \-).
.PP
\fBExamples:\fR
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx payment\-transactions refund T1 \-\-amount 3.99 \-\-currency EUR \-\-dry\-run
.fi
.RE
